Code used in Xiao
-----------------

Zen Browser desktop (https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop), MPL-2.0
  The kit makes a copy of an installed Zen; the fork overlay builds on Zen
  1.23.3b with surfer (https://github.com/zen-browser/surfer, MPL-2.0).
  shared/prefs/*.yaml uses Zen's prefs schema.

Zen Browser website (https://github.com/zen-browser/www), MPL-2.0
  site/ starts from its structure (the Astro config and i18n routing, the
  layout, theme switch and the download page's platform tabs) and follows
  zen-browser.app's page order and layout: the hero, the feature tour with its
  stack of pictures, the reveal on scroll, the dark footer with a closing
  call to download, the mobile menu, release notes with a feed. Written anew
  in plain CSS; Zen's text, images, videos and font files are not used.

Ghostery adblocker (https://github.com/ghostery/adblocker), MPL-2.0
  @ghostery/adblocker, -content and -extended-selectors are bundled in
  core/ (XiaoCore.sys.mjs and actors/XiaoChild.sys.mjs). Their bundled
  dependencies and the code they carry from others are MIT-licensed
  (tldts-experimental, Bjoern Hoehrmann's UTF-8 decoder, Lea Verou's parsel,
  Mathias Bynens' punycode); @ghostery/url-parser is MPL-2.0. esbuild writes
  every licence comment to the .LEGAL.txt file next to each bundle.

Bricolage Grotesque (https://github.com/ateliertriay/bricolage) and Junicode
(https://github.com/psb1558/Junicode-font), SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Bundled with Xiao's browser code and the website; the licence texts ship
  next to the font files (fonts/OFL-*.txt). shared/fonts/junicode-italic-
  latin.woff2 is JunicodeVF-Italic (commit 6978714) at weight 400, subset to
  Latin with fonttools. fork/branding/source/wordmark.svg is "Xiao" drawn
  from that font.

Downloaded at install time, not included in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------

Tor (https://www.torproject.org), BSD-3-Clause, with bundled components under
their own licences: the Tor Expert Bundle, only with --tor.

SearXNG (https://github.com/searxng/searxng), AGPL-3.0-or-later: only with
--search, GitHub's archive of a pinned commit, hash checked. The installer
changes the installed copy on the user's computer only: one line in
base.html links kit/search/xiao.css (MPL-2.0, Xiao's own), and Xiao's mark
replaces SearXNG's logo files. Its footer keeps the link to SearXNG's source.

Filter lists (EasyList, EasyPrivacy, uBlock Origin's lists and others, under
their own licences) and uBlock Origin's scriptlet resources (GPL-3.0): turned
into the blocking engine by scripts/build.mjs and by the website's daily
build. The engine is not kept in this repository.

Included in this repository
---------------------------

core/board/organise.js, unchanged from textarea
(https://github.com/Gitguy268/textarea, the author's own), MIT: the board
format (topics, tasks, questions) shared with textarea and the voice organiser.
Its licence is in core/board/LICENSE-organise.txt, shipped beside it.

core/bangs.json, generated by scripts/bangs.mjs from Kagi's bangs
(https://github.com/kagisearch/bangs), Copyright (c) 2024 Kagi Search, MIT, at
a pinned commit, with one name of Xiao's (!ol) added.

core/send/lib/ (nearby.js, share.js, qr.js, qr-scan.js) and core/lib/write.mjs's
tools and their wording, from textarea (https://github.com/Gitguy268/textarea,
the author's own), MIT; licence in core/send/LICENSE-textarea. core/send/vendor/:
qrcode-generator (Kazuhiko Arase) and jsQR, each with its licence beside it.

core/start/wallpaper.mjs and core/start/styles/retrofind.css, from Retrofind (the
author's own), MIT. Edge highlights in styles/glass.css after Liquid Glass Effect
by Kevin Ramirez (https://github.com/kevinbism/liquid-glass-effect), MIT.

