Ideas, no code
--------------

Brave (https://github.com/brave/brave-core), MPL-2.0: "farbling", per-site and
per-session noise on what a page can measure, and a core count no higher than
the real one. Rewritten for Firefox; none of Brave's Chromium code is used.

fingerprint-defender (https://github.com/FirstFlush/fingerprint-defender) and
browser-fingerprint-changer (https://github.com/stylishmarac/browser-fingerprint-changer),
MIT: which browser APIs to cover.

PhantomCam (https://github.com/Sententional/PhantomCam), MIT: giving a site a
picture other than your camera.

Privacy Badger (https://github.com/EFForg/privacybadger), GPL-3.0-or-later: what
privacy protection should do without being asked. Cover Your Tracks
(https://github.com/EFForg/cover-your-tracks), AGPL-3.0: linked from the start
page and used as a test against its public site; nothing from it is included.

unduck (https://github.com/t3dotgg/unduck), MIT: resolving bangs on your own
computer rather than through a search engine.

Maccy (https://github.com/p0deje/Maccy), MIT: clipboard history. Clipboard
Inspector (https://github.com/Evercoder/clipboard-inspector), MIT: showing every
format a paste holds.

BookReader (https://github.com/internetarchive/bookreader), AGPL-3.0: turning
pages of a book in one or two page views. Open Library
(https://github.com/internetarchive/openlibrary), AGPL-3.0: the !ol bang goes to
its public site.

Start page styles, ideas only: peterrauscher/startpage (Unlicense) and
caffienerd/startpage (no licence found) for a terminal prompt; GlassFox
(Ashley-Cause) and GlassyFox (AnhNguyenlost13) (no licence found), and
Safari-Golden-Gate (carlosjrrr, MIT) for glass on Firefox's own toolbars.

PDFCraft (https://github.com/PDFCraftTool/pdfcraft), AGPL-3.0: which PDF tools
to offer (pages per sheet, booklet, page numbers, crop, details, passwords,
attachments).

tab_suspender_mini (https://github.com/mawnir/tab_suspender_mini), MIT, and
Zen's former tab unloader: tab sleep after a chosen idle time, sparing the
tab on screen, pinned tabs and tabs playing sound.

Firefox Notes (https://github.com/mozilla/notes) and Websites Notes
(https://github.com/Sav22999/websites-notes), MPL-2.0: a note kept for the
site you are on.

Mullvad Browser / Tor Browser (https://github.com/mullvad/mullvad-browser),
MPL-2.0: hardening prefs in 001-base-profile.js; per-site Tor circuits and
connection isolation keys (TorDomainIsolator).

Waterfox (https://github.com/BrowserWorks/waterfox), MPL-2.0: privacy and
promotion defaults in browser/app/profile/*.js.

arkenfox user.js (https://github.com/arkenfox/user.js) and Betterfox
(https://github.com/yokoffing/Betterfox), MIT: hardening prefs; Fastfox.js
for the speed settings in shared/prefs/speed.yaml.

rapidfox (https://github.com/Eratas/rapidfox), CC0-1.0: tuning Firefox and
Zen for memory (fewer idle processes, unloading idle tabs).

chocobuckle's browser-rendering-optimisation and optimisation
(https://github.com/chocobuckle), MIT: page-speed practice on the website
(preloaded fonts, sized and lazy images, less work for sections out of view).

open-source-favicon-generation (https://github.com/rodneylab/open-source-favicon-generation),
BSD-3-Clause: the website's favicon set (SVG plus ICO, touch and manifest icons).

Archium (the author's own project): the idea of a local SearXNG for search.

The Browser Company (https://thebrowser.company): the start page's editorial
look (italic headings, off-white paper colour, soft gradients). No code,
text, images or fonts from their site are used.

Build tools
-----------

Astro, esbuild and yaml are MIT/ISC-licensed build tools. Astro's optional
image dependency sharp bundles libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later); it runs only at
build time and is not part of the website or the browser. fonttools (MIT) is
used through uvx to subset Junicode and draw the wordmark.
